# Host-specific settings for the cron scripts (collect.sh, ingest_worker.sh,
# run_*.sh). Copy to cron.env next to the scripts and fill in — cron.env is
# gitignored, so nothing host-specific ends up in this public repository.
#
#   cp cron.env.example cron.env
#
# The scripts source this file, so a plain assignment here takes precedence
# over a variable set in the crontab line. Use the ${VAR:-default} form if you
# want the caller to win instead.

# Where the export archive is written. Must be the file the web server actually
# serves: the export bakes this basename into the page as its update-manifest
# URL (yt.html -> yt.html.meta.json). Defaults to <repo>/yt.html.
EXPORT_OUTPUT=/var/www/html/yt.html

# Sync server base URL, embedded into the exported archive. REQUIRED for the
# archive's sync features: without it the export silently drops the whole
# sync UI -- login, the logged-in account display and the ingest button all
# disappear from the page. The cron scripts log a warning when it is unset.
SYNC_URL=https://sync.example.com/sync/

# Recipient for the digest mails sent by run_6hours.sh / run_12hours.sh /
# run_daily.sh. Required by those scripts — they abort if it is unset.
DIGEST_TO=you@example.com

# Channel list collect.sh falls back to when OAuth is unusable -- a missing or
# stale token.pickle, a refused refresh, a 401 on subscriptions.list. One UC...
# ID per line, '#' comments at column 0 (no inline comments -- collect.py does
# not strip them). Defaults to <repo>/channels.txt, which is gitignored: a fresh
# clone does not have it, put it on the host by hand.
# CHANNELS_FILE=/home/you/youtube-abo-summarizer/channels.txt

# Upper bound for a single collect run (any `timeout` duration). A run that
# outlives it is killed, so a stuck process cannot pile up every 30 minutes --
# and a subscription run killed this way falls back to CHANNELS_FILE, which is
# the only way to catch an OAuth browser prompt nobody will answer. Raise it
# while a large backlog is being worked off. Default: 30m.
# COLLECT_TIMEOUT=30m

# Channels that never belong in an ebook -- IDs or exact names, comma-separated.
# Read by ebook.py only: the HTML export and the mail digests keep showing every
# channel. --exclude-channel on the command line adds to this list.
# EBOOK_EXCLUDE_CHANNELS="The Daily Show,UCskip"
